  "read": "At the low #1303 camera, the old row of hanging front-left stones has settled onto the slope. Individual stone faces still read angular and the adjacent large boulder keeps its separate original downhill gap. The guardian silhouette changes little, as it should for low shingle. At the woodland gap, the bare foreground now has overlapping low leaf clusters leading to the two original spruce; from above, darker needle earth runs into separated mineral and green patches instead of a hard forest boundary. An earlier tall, straight-runners draft (04608607) read like seedlings in rows and was not selected. The revised foreground still gathers in a few bands, so the 24.47 m edge is an optional local art source rather than a recommendation to scatter it all over the island."
